{"findings":[{"title":"tenancy@1 commit reports any FeltDB failure, including an unconfirmed commit, as a CONFLICT where 'nothing was written'","severity":"medium","summary":"TenancyTransaction.commit() catches every error from db.transaction() and rethrows it as HostError CONFLICT with the message 'nothing was written'. It does not look at the error. When FeltDB answers COMMIT_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN or DURABILITY_FAILURE, the transaction may already have been applied. ArtifactHost.tenancy() awaits tx.commit() (host.ts:463), so the caller is told the membership or tenant change did not happen and that retrying is safe. A retried provision mints a fresh crypto.token tenant id and creates a second organization or membership. The collections path maps the same FeltDB codes to OUTCOME_UNKNOWN (collections.ts commitError, lines 191-196); the tenancy path does not. The new test simulates an authority that applies the write and then loses the acknowledgement: the write lands, yet commit() rejects with code CONFLICT and 'nothing was written'.","evidence":[{"kind":"code","path":"packages/appboundry-host/src/tenancy.ts","startLine":76,"endLine":80,"quote":"    try {
      await this.#db.transaction({ operations } as never);
    } catch (error) {
      throw new HostError("CONFLICT", `The membership change conflicted with a concurrent one; nothing was written. (${(error as Error).message})`);
    }"},{"kind":"code","path":"packages/appboundry-host/src/collections.ts","startLine":191,"endLine":192,"quote":"  if (error.code === FeltDBErrorCode.COMMIT_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN || error.code === FeltDBErrorCode.DURABILITY_FAILURE) {
    return new HostError("OUTCOME_UNKNOWN", `FeltDB could not confirm the commit (${error.code}); the mutation may or may not have been written.`, {"},{"kind":"check","check":"test","target":"packages/appboundry-host/test/tenancy-commit-outcome.test.ts","expect":"fails"}],"fix":"In TenancyTransaction.commit(), map FeltDB errors as commitError does. Only PRECONDITION_FAILED becomes CONFLICT ('nothing was written'). COMMIT_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN and DURABILITY_FAILURE become OUTCOME_UNKNOWN, with a hint to read before retrying. Contract violations and refusals keep their own codes, for example via feltdbRefusal/feltdbFailure. Also pass a stable transactionId so FeltDB can deduplicate a resend."}]}

